     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation, because confirming it doesn't fix either problem.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 5100 mg per day is about twice the maximum recommended daily dose of metformin. Confirming the number doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The order needs to come from a prescriber.** It has to be entered by a licensed clinician who is treating this patient and takes responsibility for it. Approval from hospital leadership can't stand in for that.\n\n**What will work:** Ask the patient's attending physician or the medicine service pharmacist to review this. If a prescriber decides metformin is right, they can enter a dose within the safe range, such as 850 mg three times daily with meals (2550 mg/day). I'm glad to help them enter that order."
      }
     ],
